[decoded] "Based on the repeated notes provided, here is a summary of how the hybrid model processes a token:\n\n*   **GatedDeltaNet Processing:** The model first passes the token through a recurrent layer where a state per value head decays over time; the key retrieves a prediction from this state, and the difference (error) between the actual value and the prediction is scaled and written back as a rank-one update to refine the state for the next query.\n*   **Full Attention Processing:** The token then passes through a standard attention layer that maintains a classic key-value cache, attending over all previous positions using partial rotary embeddings applied to only a quarter of each head.\n*   **Alternating Architecture:** These two mechanisms alternate in a specific pattern (three GatedDeltaNet layers followed by one full attention layer) to process the sequence.\n\n**Part that grows with context length:**\nThe **classic cache of keys and values** in the full attention layer grows with the length of"
